From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] apklayer: sem-clockwait-getvalue

sem_clockwait, sem_timedwait_monotonic_np and sem_getvalue unwrap the semaphore like sem_wait does. Unwrapped they resolved to glibc, which
read the stored native pointer as the semaphore: sem_clockwait returned at once and decremented the pointer, so SurfaceFlinger's OneShotTimer
threads (TouchTimer, RegSampIdle) spun at full CPU and the drifting pointer later crashed SurfaceFlinger (SIGSEGV in OneShotTimer::loop's
sem_wait, SIGBUS on a misaligned atomic: "exited: surfaceflinger (status 139/135)"). libgui and libprotobuf import sem_clockwait too.

apklayer patch 0029 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
 pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c b/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
index a520418..565312c 100644
--- a/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
+++ b/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
@@ -262,6 +262,27 @@ int bionic_sem_timedwait(bionic_sem_t *sem, const struct timespec *abs_timeout)
 	return sem_timedwait(sem->glibc, abs_timeout);
 }
 
+/* apklayer patch: the rest of bionic's semaphore API. Unwrapped, these resolve to glibc, which takes the stored native pointer for the
+ * count: sem_clockwait "succeeds" at once by decrementing the pointer (SurfaceFlinger's OneShotTimer threads spin, then crash in sem_wait). */
+int bionic_sem_clockwait(bionic_sem_t *sem, clockid_t clock, const struct timespec *abs_timeout)
+{
+	assert(sem && abs_timeout);
+	INIT_IF_NOT_MAPPED(sem, default_sem_init);
+	return sem_clockwait(sem->glibc, clock, abs_timeout);
+}
+
+int bionic_sem_timedwait_monotonic_np(bionic_sem_t *sem, const struct timespec *abs_timeout)
+{
+	return bionic_sem_clockwait(sem, CLOCK_MONOTONIC, abs_timeout);
+}
+
+int bionic_sem_getvalue(bionic_sem_t *sem, int *value)
+{
+	assert(sem && value);
+	INIT_IF_NOT_MAPPED(sem, default_sem_init);
+	return sem_getvalue(sem->glibc, value);
+}
+
